{"name":"Flax Straw","hex":"#cbaa7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flax","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Linum, especially Linum usitatissimum, which has a single, slender stalk, about a foot and a half high, with blue flowers. Also known as linseed, especially when referring to the seeds.","The fibers of Linum usitatissimum, grown to make linen and related textiles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flax"},{"term":"straw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dried stalk of a cereal plant.","Such dried stalks considered collectively; this bulk matter may be a chief salable product, a by-product, fodder, bedding, or green manure, depending on region and on current market conditions."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of straw.","Of a pale, yellowish beige colour, like that of a dried straw."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flax","blocks":[{"text":"Flax, also known as common flax or line, is a flowering plant, Linum usitatissimum, in the family Linaceae. It is cultivated as a food and fiber crop in regions of the world with temperate climates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/K%C3%B6hler%27s_Medizinal-Pflanzen_in_naturgetreuen_Abbildungen_mit_kurz_erl%C3%A4uterndem_Texte_%28Plate_16%29_BHL303594.jpg/330px-K%C3%B6hler%27s_Medizinal-Pflanzen_in_naturgetreuen_Abbildungen_mit_kurz_erl%C3%A4uterndem_Texte_%28Plate_16%29_BHL303594.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flax","wikidata":"Q45108"},{"title":"Straw","blocks":[{"text":"Straw is an agricultural byproduct consisting of the dry stalks of cereal plants after the grain and chaff have been removed. It makes up about half of the yield by weight of cereal crops such as barley, oats, rice, rye and wheat. It has a number of different uses, including fuel, livestock bedding and fodder, thatching and basket making."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Rice_straw.jpg/330px-Rice_straw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw","wikidata":"Q160066"},{"title":"Flax (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Flax or flaxen is a pale yellowish-gray, the color of straw or unspun dressed flax. The first recorded use of flax as a color name in English was in 1915, but flaxen had been used to describe hair color in David Copperfield, by Charles Dickens in 1849: Mr. Omer's granddaughter, Minnie, is described as \"a pretty little girl with long, flaxen, curling hair.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Vlasvezel.JPG/330px-Vlasvezel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flax_(color)","wikidata":"Q3746538"},{"title":"Straw (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Straw is a colour, a tone of pale yellow, the colour of straw. The Latin word stramineus, with the same meaning, is often used in describing nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strohr%C3%A4der.jpg/330px-Strohr%C3%A4der.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straw_(colour)","wikidata":"Q7622361"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Flax_flowers.jpg/500px-Flax_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Flax_flowers.jpg/960px-Flax_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Flax_flowers.jpg/500px-Flax_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlax_flowers.jpg"},{"